  "scenes": [
    {
      "caption": "Rates that pull each other along",
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "id": "s1",
      "narration": "In connected rates of change, one quantity drags another with it. As the radius of a circle grows, its area must grow too — the rate dA/dt is linked to the rate dr/dt.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "title",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 38,
            "text": "Connected rates of change",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 120
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "sub",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "one rate of change drags another with it",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 190
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "areaEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 48,
            "tex": "A = \\pi r^2",
            "x": 220,
            "y": 300
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2600,
          "do": "move",
          "dur_ms": 1000,
          "target": "areaEq",
          "to": {
            "x": 240,
            "y": 320
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "link",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "as the radius grows, the area grows with it",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 430
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5000,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "areaEq"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6200,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "A chain of rates: dA/dt follows dr/dt"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "The expanding circle",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s2",
      "narration":"A circle expands: the radius is 2 and grows at half a unit per second. Differentiating area equals pi r squared gives dA/dt equals 2 pi r dr/dt — substituting gives 2 pi, about 6.28 square units per second.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "cx": 640,
            "cy": 210,
            "fill": "none",
            "id": "pool",
            "kind": "circle",
            "r": 60,
            "stroke": "#1a1a1a",
            "strokeWidth": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "given",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 30,
            "text": "r = 2,  dr/dt = 0.5",
            "x": 540,
            "y": 320
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "dEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 40,
            "tex": "\\frac{dA}{dt} = 2\\pi r\\,\\frac{dr}{dt}",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 120
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2600,
          "do": "move",
          "dur_ms": 1000,
          "target": "dEq",
          "to": {
            "x": 120,
            "y": 140
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "ansEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "\\frac{dA}{dt} = 2\\pi(2)(0.5) = 2\\pi \\approx 6.283",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 230
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "unit",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "square units per second",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 330
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5800,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "ansEq"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7000,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "About 6.28 square units per second"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "The sliding ladder",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s3",
      "narration":"A 5-unit ladder slides down a wall, foot 3 units out and top 4 units up. Differentiating x squared plus y squared equals 25, the foot moving out at 1 unit per second means the top drops at 0.75 units per second.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "wall",
            "kind": "line",
            "stroke": "#1a1a1a",
            "width": 4,
            "x1": 120,
            "x2": 120,
            "y1": 120,
            "y2": 430
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "floor",
            "kind": "line",
            "stroke": "#1a1a1a",
            "width": 4,
            "x1": 120,
            "x2": 580,
            "y1": 430,
            "y2": 430
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "ladder",
            "kind": "line",
            "stroke": "#8a5a00",
            "width": 6,
            "x1": 320,
            "x2": 120,
            "y1": 430,
            "y2": 190
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "pyEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "x^2 + y^2 = 5^2",
            "x": 400,
            "y": 120
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "val",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "x = 3, so y = 4  (3-4-5 triangle)",
            "x": 380,
            "y": 200
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "diffEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "2x\\,\\frac{dx}{dt} + 2y\\,\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0",
            "x": 380,
            "y": 280
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "dyEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 34,
            "tex": "\\frac{dx}{dt} = 1 \\Rightarrow \\frac{dy}{dt} = -\\frac{3}{4} = -0.75",
            "x": 380,
            "y": 360
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5600,
          "do": "move",
          "dur_ms": 1400,
          "target": "ladder",
          "to": {
            "x1": 380,
            "x2": 120,
            "y1": 430,
            "y2": 240
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7400,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "dyEq"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 8600,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "The top slides down at 0.75 units per second"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "dy/dx is not a fraction",
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "id": "s4",
      "narration": "Careful: dy/dx is not a fraction whose d's can cancel. It is a single symbol for a limit — the ratio of small changes as delta x shrinks to zero. Cancel the d's and the mathematics breaks.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#b00020",
            "id": "mis",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 36,
            "text": "Misconception:",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 120
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1000,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#b00020",
            "id": "fracEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 52,
            "tex": "\\frac{dy}{dx}",
            "x": 200,
            "y": 220
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "noCancel",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 30,
            "text": "is NOT a fraction — the d's do not cancel",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 330
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "limitEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\lim_{\\delta x \\to 0} \\frac{\\delta y}{\\delta x}",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 430
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4800,
          "do": "move",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "fracEq",
          "to": {
            "x": 220,
            "y": 240
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5900,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "limitEq"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6800,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Treat dy/dx as one symbol: a rate of change"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "The connected-rates toolkit",
      "duration_ms": 7000,
      "id": "s5",
      "narration":"The toolkit is always the same: write the relation, differentiate with respect to time, then substitute the known values. The circle grew its area at 2 pi, and the ladder top fell at 0.75 units per second.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "f1",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "A = \\pi r^2 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\frac{dA}{dt} = 2\\pi r\\frac{dr}{dt}",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 140
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "f2",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "x^2 + y^2 = L^2 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x\\frac{dx}{dt} + y\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 260
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "recipe",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "differentiate each relation with respect to time",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 380
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "nums",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "circle: 2pi ≈ 6.28;   ladder top falls at 0.75",
            "x": 100,
            "y": 445
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4800,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 800,
          "target": "f1"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5800,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Differentiate the relation, substitute, solve"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "subject": "math",
  "title": "JC H2 differentiation: connected rates of change",
  "topic": "h2-differentiation"
}
